{
  "note_why": "Which MoSPI series measures each SIBC credit part (COMPOSITION_SPEC §24). One file per (credit, reference) pipeline pair, so NBFC ↔ MoSPI is another file, never code. Keyed by URN. Each part names its output series and its deflator, or a STATIC reason from core/absence.py. A series is '<dataset>/<code>' in the MoSPI CSV; output reads IIP's index or NAS's constant prices; a deflator reads a WPI/CPI index, or `implicit` = NAS current ÷ constant over the listed sectors. More than one series needs `combine`: 'sum' (NAS levels, additive as published) or 'weighted' with sourced weights. A cut's parent row inherits the cadence of the cut it is a child of (DASHBOARD_SPEC §21.4: a total row is a different signal). Checked by cross/validate_concordance.py.",
  "credit_pipeline": "sibc",
  "reference_pipeline": "mospi",
  "requires_signals": true,
